<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2"><Document><name>ILLUSTRATIVE lm2d-xichang-2026-11-26 ascent (published-knot surrogate)</name><description>FLOWN 2026-11-26. T0 is the actual liftoff 2026-11-26T09:38:00Z (+180 s from the pre-flight NET 2026-11-26T09:35:00Z). Xinhua (26 Nov 2026 18:02:36): 17:38 Beijing liftoff on a Long March 2D from Xichang, Yaogan-49 Group 01 (遥感四十九号01组卫星) reached the planned orbit, Long March flight 681. http://www.news.cn/20261126/a0282f982c184654872225d3ccb64539/c.html LL2 id b00f0e9a-48d6-4f26-9cb5-7d19169ff7c4 is Launch Successful, net 2026-11-26T09:38:00Z, minute precision, last_updated 2026-11-26T11:20:00Z. UTC columns and KML &lt;when&gt; tags shifted +180 s. Elapsed times and ECEF geometry unchanged. Sim not re-run. ILLUSTRATIVE.
ILLUSTRATIVE ASCENT ECEF — Long March 2D / Unknown Payload (Xichang LC-3) — NOT OFFICIAL TELEMETRY
PRE-FLIGHT. Unknown payload. LL2 id b00f0e9a-48d6-4f26-9cb5-7d19169ff7c4, Go, NET 2026-11-26T09:35:00Z (Thu 26 Nov 1:35 a.m. PST; 17:35 BJT), window 09:30-09:52Z, net precision Hour, last_updated 2026-11-20T09:12:38Z. Update: Added launch per NOTAMs; payload and launch vehicle identities uncertain.
Event times: SAST TYPICAL LM-2D sequence via https://sat.huijiwiki.com/wiki/长征二号丁 (same vehicle file as lm2d-taiyuan and lm2d-jiuquan): pitch-over 17.0 s, S1 cutoff 153.9 s, sep 155.1 s, fairing 185.1 s, S2 main cutoff 324.1 s, S2 vernier cutoff 705.1 s. Typical sequence, not this flight&#x27;s. Payload separation is not in this file.
Azimuth 105.51 deg: mean great-circle bearing from LL2 pad LC-3 (28.247059N 102.029008E) to the NOTAM Q-line centres. ZPKM A6099/26 centre 26 deg 49 min N, 107 deg 43 min E, bearing 104.51 deg, 583 km, valid 09:30-09:52Z (https://space-notices.com/notice/notam-ZPKM-A6099%2F26). ZGZU A6100/26 centre 25 deg 10 min N, 112 deg 08 min E, bearing 106.52 deg, 1060 km, valid 09:31-09:57Z (https://space-notices.com/notice/notam-ZGZU-A6100%2F26).
Orbit: LL2 lists Unknown and publishes no altitude. Altitude ASSUMED 500 km circular, a round LEO stand-in (same figure as lm2c-xichang when the orbit was unknown). Not an SSO target: non-rotating inclination from this azimuth is 31.91 deg. SSO at 500 km is about 97.4 deg. Circular insertion at vernier cutoff is ASSUMED.
Altitude knots (t s: km; times = published typical sequence, ALTITUDES ASSUMED = this board&#x27;s 3DOF sim at those times rounded to 0.1 km, final = ASSUMED 500 km orbit): 0:0, 17:0.3, 153.9:57.6, 155.1:58.7, 185.1:85.5, 324.1:224.3, 705.1:500
Horizontal ground speed ASSUMED linear 0 -&gt; 7.187 km/s (circular v at 500 km minus Earth rotation along Az) at T+705.1 s. File ends at final cutoff.
Pad (LL2 Launch Complex 3): 28.247059N 102.029008E. Elevation ASSUMED 0 m (LL2 gives no height; the site is well above sea level and that height is not applied). Frame: WGS-84 ECEF, positions km, velocities km/s.
Constant-azimuth rhumb Az=105.51 deg from pad, spherical R=6371.0088 km. Velocity ECEF: v_horiz along Az + hdot Up in local ENU.
T0 used: 2026-11-26T09:38:00Z. Re-run with another T0 by shifting utc_iso only; ECEF geometry is Earth-fixed.</description>
